waiver: harness-limit
reason: an aborting program is only observable as an exit code on the
  native backends. The wasm leg builds with PrintMainResult and recovers
  the exit code from a trailing stdout line, which a trapping program
  never reaches — the runner sees empty stdout and a trap, not 134. The
  interpreter reports the range and exits 1 so `fern -interp` stays
  readable, so 134 is the one code two backends agree on. Same
  restriction, and the same reason, as oob_index_read.
